    "created_at": "2018-05-31T23:02:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-31T23:02:46Z",
    "body": "> IMO if you want an array, you should not be using iterable<>. You should be using an array. iterable<> is when you need to create some completely custom collection, e.g. DOMTokenList (a type of set), URLSearchParams (a multi-map), or when you need to adapt legacy array-likes.\r\n\r\nOr when you want something that looks like an Array but actually implements the same sort of typechecking that every single other object in WebIDL is allowed to implement...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
